WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:01.164 --> 00:04.801 align:center line:79%
Recently I read of an experience
that touched me deeply.

00:05.102 --> 00:09.606 align:center line:79%
It took place at the USA Masters
Track and Field National Championship,

00:09.640 --> 00:11.475 align:center line:81%
a competition for seniors.

00:11.942 --> 00:13.343 align:center line:81%
One of the participants

00:13.343 --> 00:18.315 align:center line:79%
in the 1500 meter event was 100-
year-old Orville Rogers.

00:18.715 --> 00:23.520 align:center line:79%
The author writes: “When the starter
pistol fired, the runners took off,

00:23.754 --> 00:27.024 align:center line:79%
with Orville settling
immediately into last place,

00:27.257 --> 00:32.696 align:center line:79%
where he remained alone for the entire
race, shuffling along very slowly.

00:33.297 --> 00:35.866 align:center line:79%
[When] the last runner
besides Orville finished,

00:35.899 --> 00:38.502 align:center line:79%
Orville still had two
and a half laps to go.

00:38.902 --> 00:45.242 align:center line:79%
Nearly 3,000 spectators sat, watching
him slowly make his way around the track—

00:45.409 --> 00:49.613 align:center line:79%
completely, silently,
and uncomfortably alone.

00:50.380 --> 00:53.884 align:center line:79%
[But] when he began his final lap,
the crowd rose to their feet,

00:53.884 --> 00:55.452 align:center line:81%
cheering and applauding.

00:55.652 --> 00:57.421 align:center line:81%
By the time he hit the homestretch,

00:57.421 --> 01:01.425 align:center line:79%
the crowd was roaring. With the cheering
encouragement of thousands

01:01.425 --> 01:05.462 align:center line:79%
of spectators, Orville called
on his last reserves of energy.

01:05.963 --> 01:08.966 align:center line:79%
The crowd erupted with delight
as he crossed the finish line

01:08.966 --> 01:11.201 align:center line:81%
and was embraced by his competitors.

01:11.635 --> 01:14.671 align:center line:79%
Orville humbly and gratefully
waved to the crowd

01:14.671 --> 01:17.240 align:center line:79%
and walked off the track
with his new friends.”

01:18.175 --> 01:21.278 align:center line:79%
This was Orville's fifth race
of the competition,

01:21.511 --> 01:24.982 align:center line:79%
and in each of the other
events he had also taken last place.

01:25.549 --> 01:28.518 align:center line:79%
Some might have been tempted to judge
Orville, thinking that he shouldn't

01:28.518 --> 01:30.320 align:center line:81%
have even competed at his age,

01:30.554 --> 01:32.189 align:center line:81%
that he didn't belong on the track

01:32.189 --> 01:35.859 align:center line:79%
because he greatly prolonged
his events for everyone else.

01:36.593 --> 01:39.062 align:center line:81%
But even though he always finished last,

01:39.563 --> 01:42.866 align:center line:81%
Orville broke five world records that day.

01:43.834 --> 01:47.270 align:center line:79%
No one watching him race
would have believed that possible.

01:47.404 --> 01:51.508 align:center line:79%
But neither the spectators nor
his competitors were the judges.

01:52.109 --> 01:56.546 align:center line:79%
Orville didn't break any rules, and the
officials didn't lower any standards.

01:56.680 --> 01:59.683 align:center line:79%
He ran the same race and fulfilled
the same requirements

01:59.683 --> 02:01.518 align:center line:81%
as all the other competitors.

02:02.119 --> 02:04.321 align:center line:81%
But his degree of difficulty,

02:04.588 --> 02:07.557 align:center line:79%
in this case his age
and limited physical capacity,

02:07.557 --> 02:12.362 align:center line:79%
was factored in by placing him
in the 100+ age division.

02:12.796 --> 02:17.200 align:center line:79%
And in that division,
he broke five world records.

02:18.702 --> 02:23.607 align:center line:79%
Just as it took Orville great courage
to step out on that track each time,

02:23.874 --> 02:26.643 align:center line:79%
it also takes great courage
for some of our sisters

02:26.643 --> 02:30.280 align:center line:79%
and brothers to step
into the arena of life every day,

02:30.781 --> 02:34.184 align:center line:79%
knowing they may be judged
unfairly even though they're doing

02:34.184 --> 02:36.453 align:center line:81%
the best they can against daunting odds

02:36.453 --> 02:39.556 align:center line:79%
to follow the Savior and honor
their covenants with Him.

02:40.323 --> 02:43.460 align:center line:79%
No matter where we live
in the world, no matter our age,

02:43.794 --> 02:48.365 align:center line:79%
it is a basic human need for all
of us to feel a sense of belonging,

02:48.532 --> 02:50.367 align:center line:81%
to feel that we are wanted and needed,

02:50.567 --> 02:52.969 align:center line:79%
and that our lives
have purpose and meaning,

02:52.969 --> 02:56.373 align:center line:79%
no matter our circumstances
or limitations.

02:56.940 --> 03:01.011 align:center line:79%
On the last lap of the race, the crowd
overwhelmingly cheered Orville on,

03:01.011 --> 03:03.180 align:center line:81%
giving him the strength to keep going.

03:03.647 --> 03:08.485 align:center line:79%
It didn’t matter that he finished
last. For the participants and the crowd,

03:08.685 --> 03:11.722 align:center line:79%
this was about far
more than a competition.

03:12.155 --> 03:17.461 align:center line:79%
In many ways, this was a beautiful example
of the Savior's love in action.

03:17.828 --> 03:21.698 align:center line:79%
When Orville finished,
they all rejoiced together.

03:22.466 --> 03:24.634 align:center line:81%
Just like the masters championship,

03:24.634 --> 03:28.605 align:center line:79%
our congregations and families
can be gathering places where

03:28.605 --> 03:30.407 align:center line:81%
we cheer each other on—

03:30.741 --> 03:34.578 align:center line:79%
covenant communities fueled by the love
of Christ for one another—

03:34.878 --> 03:38.515 align:center line:79%
helping each other overcome
whatever challenges we face,

03:38.682 --> 03:42.886 align:center line:79%
giving each other strength and
encouragement without judging one another.

03:43.320 --> 03:47.657 align:center line:79%
We need each other.
Divine strength comes from unity,

03:47.657 --> 03:50.994 align:center line:79%
and that is why Satan is
intent on dividing us.

03:51.862 --> 03:53.997 align:center line:81%
Unfortunately, for some of us,

03:54.297 --> 03:58.301 align:center line:79%
attending church can be hard
at times for many different reasons.

03:58.668 --> 04:01.738 align:center line:79%
It could be someone struggling
with questions of faith,

04:01.738 --> 04:04.508 align:center line:79%
or someone with social
anxiety or depression.

04:04.975 --> 04:08.245 align:center line:79%
It could be someone from a different
country, race, or background,

04:08.245 --> 04:12.315 align:center line:79%
or someone with different life
experiences or ways of seeing things

04:12.315 --> 04:14.584 align:center line:81%
who feel they don't fit the mold.

04:15.118 --> 04:19.322 align:center line:79%
It could be someone mustering the courage
to return after years of being away,

04:19.689 --> 04:23.093 align:center line:79%
or someone with a nagging
feeling that they just don't measure up

04:23.093 --> 04:24.494 align:center line:81%
and will never belong.

04:25.162 --> 04:29.566 align:center line:79%
It could even be sleep deprived and
emotionally stretched parents of babies

04:29.566 --> 04:35.806 align:center line:79%
and young children, or someone that’s
single in a congregation full of marrieds—

04:36.373 --> 04:38.408 align:center line:81%
of families and couples.

04:39.075 --> 04:44.281 align:center line:79%
President Russell M. Nelson has said,
“If a couple in your ward gets divorced,

04:44.281 --> 04:49.419 align:center line:79%
or a young missionary returns home early,
or a teenager doubts his testimony,

04:49.719 --> 04:51.922 align:center line:81%
they do not need your judgment.

04:52.489 --> 04:56.526 align:center line:79%
They need to experience the pure love
of Jesus Christ reflected

04:56.526 --> 04:58.562 align:center line:81%
in your words and actions.”

04:59.329 --> 05:03.600 align:center line:79%
Our experience at church is meant
to provide vital connections with the Lord

05:03.600 --> 05:07.137 align:center line:79%
and with each other that are so
needed for our spiritual

05:07.137 --> 05:08.471 align:center line:81%
and emotional well-being.

05:09.105 --> 05:11.608 align:center line:79%
Inherent in the covenants
we make with God,

05:11.675 --> 05:15.645 align:center line:79%
beginning with baptism, is
our responsibility to love

05:15.645 --> 05:19.115 align:center line:79%
and care for each other
as members of the family of God,

05:19.115 --> 05:20.951 align:center line:81%
members of the body of Christ,

05:21.251 --> 05:25.622 align:center line:79%
and not just to check off a box
on a list of things we’re expected to do.

05:26.189 --> 05:29.626 align:center line:79%
Christlike love and care
are higher and holier.

05:30.060 --> 05:32.529 align:center line:81%
The pure love of Christ is charity.

05:33.029 --> 05:34.764 align:center line:81%
As President Nelson said,

05:35.232 --> 05:39.836 align:center line:79%
“Charity propels us ’to bear one
another’s burdens’ rather than heap

05:39.836 --> 05:41.605 align:center line:81%
burdens upon each other.”

05:42.305 --> 05:47.344 align:center line:79%
The Savior said, “By this shall all
men know that ye are my disciples,

05:47.711 --> 05:50.313 align:center line:81%
if ye have love one to another.”

05:50.847 --> 05:52.616 align:center line:81%
And President Nelson added,

05:52.816 --> 05:57.988 align:center line:79%
“Charity is the principal characteristic
of a true follower of Jesus Christ.”

05:58.388 --> 06:00.223 align:center line:81%
“The Savior’s message is clear:

06:00.490 --> 06:05.562 align:center line:79%
His true disciples build, lift,
encourage, persuade, and inspire ....

06:05.562 --> 06:08.531 align:center line:79%
How we speak to and about
others ... really matters.”

06:09.065 --> 06:11.368 align:center line:79%
The Savior's teaching
on this is very simple.

06:11.368 --> 06:14.571 align:center line:79%
It’s summed up in the Golden
Rule: “Do unto others

06:14.571 --> 06:16.473 align:center line:81%
as you would have others do unto you.”

06:16.973 --> 06:19.175 align:center line:81%
Put yourself in that person's place

06:19.175 --> 06:23.546 align:center line:79%
and treat them the way you would want
to be treated if you were in their shoes.

06:24.180 --> 06:28.351 align:center line:79%
Christlike treatment of others goes
far beyond our families and congregations,

06:28.585 --> 06:32.923 align:center line:79%
it includes our sisters and brothers
of other faiths or no faith at all.

06:33.590 --> 06:37.894 align:center line:79%
It includes our brothers and sisters
from other countries and cultures,

06:37.894 --> 06:41.264 align:center line:79%
as well as those of other
political persuasions.

06:41.731 --> 06:46.336 align:center line:79%
We are all part of the family
of God, and He loves all His children.

06:46.670 --> 06:51.207 align:center line:79%
He desires that His children
love Him and also one another.

06:51.775 --> 06:55.412 align:center line:79%
The Savior’s life was an example
of loving, gathering, and lifting,

06:55.412 --> 06:58.715 align:center line:79%
even those who society had judged
as outcasts and unclean.

06:59.249 --> 07:01.851 align:center line:79%
His is an example
we are commanded to follow.

07:02.152 --> 07:04.621 align:center line:79%
We are here to develop
Christlike attributes

07:04.621 --> 07:06.856 align:center line:81%
and eventually become like our Savior.

07:07.324 --> 07:09.926 align:center line:81%
His is not a gospel of checklists;

07:10.193 --> 07:12.262 align:center line:81%
it is a gospel of becoming—

07:12.662 --> 07:16.032 align:center line:81%
becoming as He is and loving as He does.

07:16.366 --> 07:18.902 align:center line:81%
He wants us to become a Zion people.

07:19.369 --> 07:23.907 align:center line:79%
When I was in my late 20s, I went
through a period of deep depression,

07:23.907 --> 07:25.342 align:center line:81%
and during that time it was

07:25.342 --> 07:29.412 align:center line:79%
as if the reality that God
existed was suddenly gone.

07:29.946 --> 07:34.884 align:center line:79%
I can't fully explain the feeling
other than to say I felt completely lost.

07:35.418 --> 07:37.654 align:center line:81%
From the time I was a young child,

07:37.954 --> 07:40.991 align:center line:79%
I had always known that my Father
in Heaven was there

07:40.991 --> 07:42.625 align:center line:81%
and that I could talk to Him.

07:43.093 --> 07:47.664 align:center line:79%
But during that time,
I no longer knew if there was a God.

07:48.331 --> 07:51.534 align:center line:79%
I'd never experienced anything like
that before in my life,

07:51.534 --> 07:54.771 align:center line:79%
and it felt like my whole
foundation was crumbling.

07:55.271 --> 07:58.308 align:center line:79%
As a result, it was hard
for me to attend church.

07:58.608 --> 08:00.210 align:center line:81%
I went, but it was partly

08:00.210 --> 08:04.280 align:center line:79%
because I was afraid of being labeled
inactive or less faithful,

08:04.614 --> 08:08.518 align:center line:79%
and I was afraid of becoming
someone’s assigned project.

08:08.952 --> 08:12.789 align:center line:79%
What I really needed during that
time was to feel genuine love,

08:12.856 --> 08:16.793 align:center line:79%
understanding, and support from
those around me, not judgment.

08:17.127 --> 08:20.430 align:center line:79%
Some of the assumptions I was afraid
people would make about me,

08:20.864 --> 08:25.635 align:center line:79%
I myself had made about others when
they didn't regularly attend church.

08:25.635 --> 08:28.805 align:center line:79%
That painful personal
experience taught me some valuable

08:28.805 --> 08:32.976 align:center line:79%
lessons about why we’ve been commanded not
to judge one another

08:32.976 --> 08:38.148 align:center line:79%
unrighteously. Are there
those who among us who suffer in silence,

08:38.548 --> 08:41.084 align:center line:79%
afraid for others
to know their hidden struggles

08:41.084 --> 08:44.354 align:center line:79%
because they don't know
what the reaction will be?

08:44.354 --> 08:47.791 align:center line:79%
Only the Lord fully knows
the actual level of difficulty with

08:47.791 --> 08:50.360 align:center line:79%
which each of us is running
our race of life—

08:50.760 --> 08:52.429 align:center line:81%
the burdens, the challenges,

08:52.429 --> 08:56.933 align:center line:79%
and the obstacles we face
that often cannot be seen by others.

08:57.434 --> 09:00.703 align:center line:79%
Only He fully understands
the life-changing wounds

09:00.703 --> 09:03.339 align:center line:81%
and trauma some of us may have experienced

09:03.339 --> 09:06.910 align:center line:79%
in the past that are still
affecting us in the present.

09:07.444 --> 09:09.612 align:center line:81%
Often we even judge ourselves harshly,

09:09.612 --> 09:13.049 align:center line:79%
thinking we should be much
farther ahead on the track.

09:13.049 --> 09:17.220 align:center line:79%
Only the Lord fully knows our individual
limitations and capacity.

09:17.587 --> 09:20.690 align:center line:79%
And because of that,
He is the only one fully qualified

09:20.690 --> 09:22.258 align:center line:81%
to judge our performance.

09:22.625 --> 09:23.860 align:center line:81%
Sisters and brothers,

09:23.860 --> 09:25.995 align:center line:79%
let's be like those spectators
in the story

09:25.995 --> 09:29.065 align:center line:79%
and cheer each other on in
our journey of discipleship,

09:29.165 --> 09:31.234 align:center line:81%
no matter our circumstances.

09:31.534 --> 09:35.171 align:center line:79%
That doesn’t require us to break
rules or lower standards. It’s

09:35.472 --> 09:40.844 align:center line:79%
actually the second great commandment—
to love our neighbor as ourselves.

09:41.311 --> 09:42.946 align:center line:81%
And as our Savior has said,

09:43.213 --> 09:46.382 align:center line:79%
“Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one
of the least of these ...,

09:46.950 --> 09:48.451 align:center line:81%
ye have done it unto me,”

09:48.952 --> 09:56.192 align:center line:79%
for good or for ill. He has also told us,
“If you’re not one, ye are not mine.”

09:56.993 --> 09:58.294 align:center line:81%
There will be times in each

09:58.294 --> 10:01.598 align:center line:79%
of our lives when we will be the ones
who need help and encouragement.

10:01.598 --> 10:05.869 align:center line:79%
Let’s commit now to always do
that for each other. As we do,

10:05.935 --> 10:08.037 align:center line:81%
we will develop greater unity

10:08.037 --> 10:13.042 align:center line:79%
and facilitate a space for the Savior
to do His sacred work of healing

10:13.042 --> 10:14.844 align:center line:81%
and transforming each of us.

10:15.545 --> 10:19.883 align:center line:79%
To those of you who may feel you have
lagged far behind in this race of life,

10:19.883 --> 10:23.353 align:center line:79%
this journey of mortality,
please keep going.

10:23.887 --> 10:27.190 align:center line:79%
Only the Savior can fully judge
where you should be at this point,

10:27.190 --> 10:29.826 align:center line:81%
and He is compassionate and just.

10:30.160 --> 10:32.495 align:center line:81%
He is the great judge of the race of life,

10:32.495 --> 10:36.766 align:center line:79%
and the only one who fully
understands the level of difficulty with

10:36.766 --> 10:40.370 align:center line:79%
which you are running,
or walking, or shuffling.

10:40.870 --> 10:44.040 align:center line:79%
He will take into account
your limitations, your capacity,

10:44.073 --> 10:45.808 align:center line:81%
your life experiences,

10:45.808 --> 10:50.446 align:center line:79%
and the hidden burdens you carry
as well as the desires of your heart.

10:50.914 --> 10:55.185 align:center line:79%
You may actually be breaking
symbolic world records as well.

10:55.585 --> 10:57.086 align:center line:81%
Please don't lose hope.

10:57.086 --> 10:59.589 align:center line:81%
Please keep going. Please stay.

10:59.989 --> 11:04.060 align:center line:79%
You do belong. The Lord
needs you, and we need you.

11:04.627 --> 11:08.565 align:center line:79%
Wherever you live in the world,
no matter how remote it may be,

11:08.631 --> 11:11.067 align:center line:79%
please always remember
that your Father in Heaven

11:11.067 --> 11:14.704 align:center line:79%
and your Savior know you
completely and love you perfectly.

11:14.704 --> 11:16.806 align:center line:81%
You are never forgotten to Them.

11:17.073 --> 11:18.775 align:center line:81%
They want to bring you home.

11:19.175 --> 11:20.710 align:center line:81%
Keep your eye on the Savior.

11:20.710 --> 11:23.313 align:center line:81%
He is your iron rod. Don’t let go of Him.

11:23.513 --> 11:26.716 align:center line:79%
I testify that He lives
and that you can trust Him.

11:26.916 --> 11:30.687 align:center line:81%
I also testify that He is cheering you on.

11:30.954 --> 11:35.425 align:center line:79%
May we all follow the Savior's example
and cheer each other on, is my prayer.

11:35.425 --> 11:37.827 align:center line:81%
In the name of Jesus Christ, amen.

